Z||000012||filthyscarecrow||11-19-2001||10:51 PM||||well, maybe mine aren't rice after all...<BR>i just changed from the "light bar" across the back to 3 individual red ovals on each side plus backup lights. they're recessed into the bumper too. i just took a bunch of pics, i have to get them developed (yeah, yeah, i know.) but i'll post em as soon as i have em.||||reg||1
Z||000013||AusFiero||11-20-2001||07:33 AM||||Well this is probably a good place o post this. I have been talking to a manufacturer of lenses and complete lighting units. He is a low volume supplier and as long as there is 10 orders for something he makes them. <BR>I threw this idea at him yesterday. See Pic.<BR>If 10 people show interest I can get them made in late January when he has the equipment big enough to handle the large Fiero lenses. He can also reproduce them in the original red and orange. or red and white even.<BR>Cost is the decider. I would have to sell them for US$220 a pair. Any interest? <BR>Smaller lights can also be made easily and I have been talking to him about doing Fiero front markers and even side marke lights in clear. Again it has to be an order of 10.<BR>I dropped my MR2 front lights to him today to start selling them also in clear as they are super expensive. They will sell for about $99 a set which is good compared to the $180 a set I see them on ebay for.<P>I could do an Altezza style light next year some time but again I would need at least 10 orders and they would not be cheap. Probably about $500 a pair.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierotaillightclear.jpg">  <P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero4.gif">      <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000014||Nashco||11-20-2001||09:00 AM||||That looks gorgeous Aus!  That's what I plan on doing with my reflectors after I do the clear tails like MinnGreen's.  The solid clear is just temporary, but I want the lines like you've got, I really like the look.  Unfortunately, I'm one of those guys that's too poor and cheap to buy it, I'm going to try and do it myself.  That sounds like a fair price, since a set of used stock reflectors cost about 40 bucks.<P>The Altezzas...that would really interest me to see, but again, WAY out of my budget.  I'm almost positive that you could sell 10 of those taillight lense sets.  If my attempt doesn't work out, or if it will take me longer than expected, the 220 bucks is a great deal.<P>Hopefully I'm not the only one who thinks they're cool, but since all of your other ideas have been immensely popular, I'm sure this one will be too!<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000015||MinnGreenGT||11-20-2001||09:56 AM||||AUS!!! That's great!  That's exactly what I was working for when I started my clear taillight project... just seemed like too much work to do by hand.  Wow!  That's Awsome. How did they make 'em?  (I couldn't come up with an easy way).  And I'd definitely be interested in a set of clear marker lights all around (I don't feel like developing them myself...and you seem to have a good connection.  <P>I'd still seriously be interested in an Altezza sytle light set down the road a bit (I just sold my '84SE to finance a set of Stage-2 scoops).||||reg||1
Z||000016||ChopTop||11-20-2001||10:21 AM||||What set's the Altezza tail lights and similar ones apart isn't the clear covers, but the chrome surrounding the oval red lens.  .  <BR>I could see using the original clear Fiero covers, but you would have to develop a complete new piece to fit inside the covers, be plastic chromed, and then have a red lens style incorporated into them to achieve the Altezza look.||||reg||1
Z||000017||Haze_Performance||11-20-2001||11:57 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by AusFiero:<BR><B>Well this is probably a good place o post this. I have been talking to a manufacturer of lenses and complete lighting units. He is a low volume supplier and as long as there is 10 orders for something he makes them. <BR>I threw this idea at him yesterday. See Pic.<BR>If 10 people show interest I can get them made in late January when he has the equipment big enough to handle the large Fiero lenses. He can also reproduce them in the original red and orange. or red and white even.<BR>Cost is the decider. I would have to sell them for US$220 a pair. Any interest? <BR>Smaller lights can also be made easily and I have been talking to him about doing Fiero front markers and even side marke lights in clear. Again it has to be an order of 10.<BR>I dropped my MR2 front lights to him today to start selling them also in clear as they are super expensive. They will sell for about $99 a set which is good compared to the $180 a set I see them on ebay for.<P>I could do an Altezza style light next year some time but again I would need at least 10 orders and they would not be cheap. Probably about $500 a pair.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierotaillightclear.jpg">   <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Once again Aus... GREAT JOB!!! Will he make Altezza type lights for a notchback? If so is there a photoshop rendering of what they would look like? (hint-hint)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> I really would like a set of the Altezza type, without the chrome. Maybe with a black (Not carbon fiber) painted inside. Thanks & keep up the great work..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/goodlife.gif">    <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="purple">Goto Website - <A HREF="http://www.ClassicFiero.com" TARGET=_blank>Click Here</A> </FONT></FONT>||||reg||14
