Z||000021||AusFiero||11-20-2001||04:26 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MinnGreenGT:<BR><B>AUS!!! That's great!  That's exactly what I was working for when I started my clear taillight project... just seemed like too much work to do by hand.  Wow!  That's Awsome. How did they make 'em?  (I couldn't come up with an easy way).  And I'd definitely be interested in a set of clear marker lights all around (I don't feel like developing them myself...and you seem to have a good connection.  <P>I'd still seriously be interested in an Altezza sytle light set down the road a bit (I just sold my '84SE to finance a set of Stage-2 scoops).</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The guy wont give to many of his manufacturing methods away but the money saved is in the moulds he uses to cast the lights. The above would be cast in one piece as original. He does a lot of lights for the reproduction market and does all of Australias amber lenses for Corvettes as required here.<P>Haze. I will see what I can whip up. I actually like the look of the Altezza style myself in the black rather than chrome. Chroming plastic is very expensive. <P>Hybrid. They look great. You have my brain ticking now  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero4.gif">      <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
